\section{Participants}
\label{sec:method_participants}
Twenty-eight participants were recruited ($N=28$; 14 female, 14 male). Participants needed normal or corrected-to-normal vision and no history of neurological disorders. Much of the recruitment ran through university mailing lists. The sample therefore skews toward an academically oriented population (Sections~\ref{sec:conclusion} and~\ref{sec:future_research}).

Before the main recordings, three pilot sessions (P1--P3) tested the recording and analysis pipeline. P1 is a recording of the author and experiment lead. P2 and P3 are recordings of two other people. The pilot sessions are not part of the sample. The recruited participants therefore carry the IDs P4--P31.

Three recruited participants were excluded before analysis. P16 and P19 each reported more than 10 keypress errors: 45 and 40 swipes without a keypress. A swipe without a keypress leaves no time mark. The seconds before that swipe would then count as \texttt{STAY} instead of \texttt{SKIP}. P29 reported a diagnosed neurological disorder in the pre-session survey. Figure~\ref{fig:participant_inclusion} shows the selection.

