The author set Guided Access to 25 minutes in the TikTok app. The author told participants that a Bluetooth dropout needs no action: participants should keep browsing, and the recording pipeline reconnects by itself (Section~\ref{sec:method_data_acquisition}). Participants then browsed alone in the room, with the door closed, so that responses to the feed could stay natural. In case of problems, participants could knock on the glass door. No major interruption occurred.

After 25 minutes, the author entered the room, and the participant took off the headband. In a short post-session survey, participants reported their keypress errors (Section~\ref{sec:method_participants}). Paid participants then signed the forms for the voucher (Section~\ref{sec:method_participants}). The post-session survey, the forms and the debrief took about two to four minutes. The author thanked participants and, on request, explained the wider context of the study.

