\section{Feature Engineering}
\label{sec:method_feature_engineering}
Feature engineering turns each 1.0~s window (Section~\ref{sec:method_windowing}) into 236 numbers, called \emph{features} (executed via \url{https://github.com/coffeeandcoffee/eeg_tiktok_pipeline/blob/main/data_analysis/step05_feature_engineering.py}). The 236 features form two groups:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Band features:} eight features for each of the seven bands at each of the four electrodes, \(7 \times 4 \times 8 = 224\) features. The eight band features are mean, standard deviation, Relative Power, the three Hjorth parameters, Peak Frequency and Macro Frequency.
    \item \textbf{Raw features:} three features of the raw signal at each of the four electrodes, \(4 \times 3 = 12\) features. The three raw features are mean, standard deviation and slope.
\end{itemize}
The EI is computed separately from the same windows and serves as the benchmark for the 236 features.

Every band feature is computed on \(y(t)\), the z-scored envelope of one band at one electrode within one window (Equation~\ref{eq:zscore}). The window holds \(N\) samples and lasts \(T\) seconds. A full window has \(N = 256\) and \(T = 1.0\)~s. The 531 shortened windows at the end of a stretch hold fewer samples (Section~\ref{sec:method_windowing}).

\subsection{Mean, Standard Deviation and Relative Power}
The mean of \(y(t)\) gives the level of the band strength within the window. The standard deviation of \(y(t)\) gives the spread of the band strength within the window. Figure~\ref{fig:stat_moments} shows the mean and the standard deviation for one window. The 236 features do not include the minimum and the maximum of \(y(t)\). The value of the minimum and the maximum as features is left to future research and lies beyond the scope of the present thesis.

Relative Power divides the mean of one band by the sum of the means of all seven bands at the same electrode. The means are z-scores and can be negative. Relative Power is therefore no share of total power, although the name suggests one. When the sum of the seven means is zero or negative, Relative Power is set to 0. Across all windows, Relative Power is 0 in 40\% of the values and negative in 20\%.

