\subsection{Temporal Cross-Validation and Data Balancing}
Two settings test the models. The \emph{intra-subject} setting trains and tests one model per participant, as Nuamah et al.\ and McCartney et al.\ do (Sections~\ref{sec:engagement_definitions} and~\ref{sec:lit_parameter_choice}). The \emph{inter-subject} setting trains one model on 24 participants and tests the model on the 25th participant, once for every participant (Leave-One-Group-Out cross-validation, with one participant per group). A test on a new participant shows whether a result holds beyond the participants in the training data \cite{varoquaux_assessing_2017}.

The intra-subject setting uses blocked temporal 5-fold cross-validation (executed via \url{https://github.com/coffeeandcoffee/eeg_tiktok_pipeline/blob/main/data_analysis/step04_balance_split.py}). Neighbouring windows of one recording look alike. A test window right next to a training window would let the model recognise the test window instead of predicting the class, much like a student who has seen the exam questions during practice (Section~\ref{sec:adjacent_studies}). Varoquaux et al.\ therefore call for a time separation between training data and test data, and for cross-validation on whole blocks of correlated data \cite{varoquaux_assessing_2017}.

The pipeline cuts the windows of each participant, in time order, into five folds. The fold borders sit where each fold holds about one fifth of the \texttt{SKIP} windows of the participant (Figure~\ref{fig:5_fold_split_per_participant}). Each fold serves once as test data, while the other four folds serve as training data.

At each fold border, the pipeline drops every window that starts within 1.5~s of the border. The present thesis calls the dropped 3~s the \emph{fold gap}. The start of every training window therefore lies more than 3~s from the start of every test window. A window lasts 1.0~s, so more than 2~s without any window separate a training window from a test window. The author set the 3~s; Varoquaux et al.\ give no value. The pipeline checks the fold gap in every fold and stops with an error when a training window and a test window start less than 2.9~s apart, 3~s minus a tolerance of 0.1~s. No fold triggered the check (Figure~\ref{fig:3s_fold_boundary}). Figure~\ref{fig:fold_boundaries_for_one_participant} shows the five folds and the four fold gaps of one participant.

