The present section compares the class separation of the EI with the class separation of the 236 features. Class separation is measured as \(|d|\) (Section~\ref{sec:method_feature_separation_cohen_d}). The EI reaches \(|d| = 0.022\). All \(|d|\) values in the present section lie under 0.2, the value Cohen gives for a small effect \cite{cohen_statistical_1988}, come from one dataset and carry no statistical test.

Figure~\ref{fig:cohend_by_freq_band} shows the mean \(|d|\) per band. Every band and the raw signal lie above the EI. Alpha lies lowest, close to the EI. High gamma lies highest, about 0.03 above the EI. Only four signals exceed 0.04: the raw signal, delta, low gamma and high gamma. The raw signal ranks second, behind high gamma.

Across the bands, \(|d|\) does not rise or fall steadily with frequency. \(|d|\) is high at delta, dips to the lowest value at alpha, peaks at high gamma and falls again at very high gamma. Section~\ref{sec:results_interpretation} discusses delta.

